/build
.DS_Store
/node_modules

# dist/ is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# The built admin bundle is committed so that installing this package needs no
# Node at all: composer require, vendor:publish, done. On a 1 vCPU / 1GB box
# that is not a convenience, it is the difference between deploying and running
# out of memory partway through a Vite build.
#
# The cost is noisy diffs and a discipline requirement to rebuild before
# tagging. `php artisan cms:admin-assets --check` fails when dist/ is older
# than resources/js, so CI can enforce it rather than trusting memory.
#
# The dev server's hot file is a local artefact and is never committed.
/dist/hot
